# 11. ONE_OF / ALL_OF SEMANTICS

This is a major acceptance criterion.

Some criteria have:

- Mandatory requirements.
- Alternative forms of evidence.
- ONE_OF requirement groups.
- ALL_OF requirement groups.

Example:

One qualifying option out of four may be sufficient.

The Student may submit additional achievements voluntarily.

The reviewer should not need to reject every undeclared optional alternative.

Audit whether the current system:

- Requires assessing undeclared alternatives.
- Treats empty optional fields as failures.
- Blocks criterion completion unnecessarily.
- Overcounts declaration requirements.
- Requires duplicate conclusion clicks.

Determine how the actual policy evaluates each criterion.

Document the correct human review completion rules.

Do not change eligibility rules merely to make progress appear complete.

